@title Q4 DR Drill: Scheduling
@subtitle Runbook and results from the quarterly disaster recovery drill
@author Platform Resilience, Bramble Health
@date 2026-10-07

kpi RTO | 74 min | +14 min vs target | bad
kpi RPO | 9 min | -6 min vs target | good
kpi Smoke tests | 46 of 48 | -2 vs target | bad
kpi Data verified | 100% | on target | good

# Scope
Restore the patient-scheduling service in us-east-2 from backups after simulating the loss of us-west-2.

# Restore procedure
1. Freeze writes in us-west-2.
2. Restore the latest RDS snapshot in us-east-2.
3. Restore the S3 attachments bucket from the replica.
4. Deploy the service stack from the release tag.
!! Confirm the snapshot timestamp before switching DNS. Promoting an old snapshot silently loses appointments.
5. Switch DNS for `scheduling.bramble.example` to us-east-2.
6. Run the smoke test suite.
7. Reopen writes.

# Results
table = Metric,Target,Achieved; RTO,60 minutes,**74 minutes**; RPO,15 minutes,9 minutes; Smoke tests passed,48 of 48,**46 of 48**; Data verified,100 percent,100 percent

data phases = phase,minutes; Snapshot restore,31; S3 restore,12; Stack deploy,18; DNS switch,6; Smoke tests,7
chart bar phases y=minutes unit=min labels title="Minutes spent per phase"

Snapshot restore took 31 of the 74 minutes and is the main reason the drill missed its RTO target.

# Follow-ups
- Pre-provision the database subnet group in us-east-2 to cut restore time.
- Fix the 2 smoke tests that depend on a us-west-2-only endpoint.
- Automate the DNS switch with a health-checked failover record.
- Next drill on 2027-01-20.
